WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.899 --> 00:00:04.950
Two contracts can look similar and create
very different operating commitments.

2
00:00:05.763 --> 00:00:09.763
Here, the analyst matches nine
terms across Growth and Enterprise,

3
00:00:10.157 --> 00:00:13.347
then makes the service-level
differences visible side by side.

4
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.971
The follow-up moves beyond response time.

5
00:00:18.323 --> 00:00:21.939
Maintenance notice, billing
disputes, API availability,

6
00:00:22.206 --> 00:00:24.499
and latency all affect how teams work.

7
00:00:24.979 --> 00:00:26.618
Scrolling through the comparison reveals

8
00:00:26.643 --> 00:00:29.053
the details that a headline
summary could miss.

9
00:00:31.262 --> 00:00:33.005
Every comparison needs its source.

10
00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:36.414
Section three point two
confirms the response targets.

11
00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:39.230
The credit clauses show why context matters:

12
00:00:39.624 --> 00:00:43.572
the caps differ, but so do the conditions
that make those remedies available.

13
00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.019
The output becomes a
practical review checklist.

14
00:00:48.541 --> 00:00:50.408
Legal verifies executed terms.

15
00:00:50.845 --> 00:00:53.352
The service owner maps
obligations to controls.

16
00:00:53.704 --> 00:00:55.428
Any mismatch is assessed against

17
00:00:55.453 --> 00:00:58.119
the applicable conditions
before a decision is made.

18
00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:01.787
The value is in connecting the
wording to the work it requires.
